# OTP Unverified Call List — client integration guide

Admin API for users who **requested OTP** in a date window but **did not successfully verify after that request**. Use this list to call numbers and ask what blocked verification (SMS delay, wrong OTP, app crash, etc.).

**Related:**
- [`FRONTEND_ADMIN_API_CONTRACT.md`](./FRONTEND_ADMIN_API_CONTRACT.md) — auth, base URL
- [`LOGIN_FUNNEL_CLIENT.md`](./LOGIN_FUNNEL_CLIENT.md) — OTP requested / verified totals
- `/analytics/otp` — request / success / fail counts with daily series

---

## Summary

| Item | Detail |
|------|--------|
| Endpoint | `GET /api/admin/analytics/otp-unverified` |
| Auth | Admin Bearer JWT (`ROLE_ADMIN`) |
| Purpose | Paginated call list of OTP dropoffs |
| Collection | `auth_info` |
| Window | `[start, end)` on `lastOtpRequestedAt` |
| Default range | Last **7 days** ending at `now` |
| Sort | `lastOtpRequestedAt` descending |

---

## Cohort

A row is included when **all** of:

1. `lastOtpRequestedAt` in `[start, end)`
2. Latest request not verified: `otpVerifiedAt` is **null**, **or** `otpVerifiedAt < lastOtpRequestedAt`
3. `accountStatus != DELETED`

Includes:

- First-time users who never verified
- Returning users who requested OTP again and did not finish verify after that request

---

## Why this is not `otp_requested − otp_success`

`/analytics/otp` counts:

| Metric | Field in range |
|--------|----------------|
| `otp_requested` | `lastOtpRequestedAt` |
| `otp_success` | `otpVerifiedAt` |

Those are **different timestamps**, not a nested funnel. A user can request in the window and verify outside it (or the reverse). This endpoint answers: “who requested in this window and still hasn’t verified **that** request?”

---

## Endpoint

```
GET /api/admin/analytics/otp-unverified
```

### Query parameters

| Param | Type | Required | Default | Description |
|-------|------|----------|---------|-------------|
| `start` | Instant (ISO-8601) | No | `end − 7 days` | Inclusive lower bound on `lastOtpRequestedAt` |
| `end` | Instant (ISO-8601) | No | `now` | Exclusive upper bound |
| `page` | int | No | `0` | Zero-based page |
| `size` | int | No | `20` | Page size, **max 100** |

`400` when resolved `start` is not strictly before `end`.

### Example requests

```http
GET /api/admin/analytics/otp-unverified
GET /api/admin/analytics/otp-unverified?start=2026-09-20T00:00:00Z&end=2026-09-26T00:00:00Z&page=0&size=50
```

